  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One and CX-1 through a series of target interactions. This compound is implicated in the target of multiple entities, including VMRC-LCP, which is a target of NRF2 activator Geopyxin F, and also of Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, which in turn targets CX-1. Similarly, Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One is also a target of Isoamyl isobutyrate, which also targets CX-1. These findings indicate that Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One may act as a central node in a network of targets that ultimately lead to the activation of CX-1. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanisms by which these interactions occur remain to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible pathway where Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One may influence CX-1 through intermediate targets, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
